Fix RDRAM initialization (upstream mupen64plus-core b4d028a, backported)

The RDRAM registers were addressed by guesswork ("pure guessing, need
hardware test" in ri_controller.h), and the module that a register access
reaches was decided by hacks keyed on the IPL3's own register writes. Boot
code that initialises the memory chips the way the hardware documents it,
rather than the way Nintendo's IPL3 happens to, found no memory at all.
libdragon's open-source IPL3 (every libdragon ROM built since 2023) is such
code: it detected 0 MB, placed its second stage below the start of RAM and
jumped into unmapped memory, and our app hung on the game's first frame.

This is upstream's own fix (mupen64plus/mupen64plus-core, PR #1111, merged
2025-04-30), which libretro carries in mupen64plus-libretro-nx since its
2026-09-18 core sync. RDRAM addressing follows n64brew's documentation, the
"corrupted read" handler is switched on the calibration state of the modules
instead of on two IPL3 register writes, and the two save-state loaders that
rebuild module ids use the new addressing. The save-state FORMAT is
unchanged: the same registers are written and read.

Applied at build time by Vendor/n64-ios/build.sh, after 0005.

diff --git a/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ri/ri_controller.h b/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ri/ri_controller.h
index 940fa80..852cb6f 100644
--- a/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ri/ri_controller.h
+++ b/mupen64plus-core/src/device/rcp/ri/ri_controller.h
@@ -54,12 +54,23 @@ static osal_inline uint32_t ri_reg(uint32_t address)
     return (address & 0xffff) >> 2;
 }
 
-static osal_inline uint16_t ri_address_to_id_field(uint32_t address)
+static osal_inline uint32_t ri_address(uint32_t address)
 {
-    /* XXX: pure guessing, need harware test */
-    return (uint16_t)(((address >> 20) == 0x03f)
-        ? (address & 0x0007fc00) >> 10   /* RDRAM registers id_field: [19..10] */
-        : (address & 0x00f00000) >> 20); /* RDRAM memory    id_field: [23..20] */
+    /* https://n64brew.dev/wiki/RDRAM_Interface#Memory_addressing */
+    return (((address >> 20) == 0x03f)
+        ? (((address & 0x3ff)))              | /* Adr[10:0]  */
+           (((address >> 10) & 0x1ff) << 11) | /* Adr[19:11] */
+           (((address >> 10) & 0x1ff) << 20)   /* Adr[28:20] */
+        : (((address & 0x7ff)))              | /* Adr[10:0]  */
+           (((address >> 11) & 0x1ff) << 11) | /* Adr[19:11] */
+           (((address >> 20) & 0x03f) << 20)); /* Adr[28:20] */
+}
+
+static osal_inline uint16_t ri_address_to_id_field(uint32_t address, uint8_t swapfield)
+{
+    /* https://n64brew.dev/wiki/RDRAM#RDRAM_addressing */
+    return (((swapfield  & ((address >> 11) & 0x1ff))) 
+          | ((~swapfield & ((address >> 20) & 0x1ff)))); /* AdrS[28:20] */
 }
 
 
